commit 56214838a55fb6f3f32c2b880ff43ee026c3dbe0
Author: Scott Sunarto <github@smsunarto.com>
Date:   Mon Nov 16 04:07:16 2026 -0800

    build: cache each package's typecheck with incremental tsc
    
    Each typecheck script writes its .tsbuildinfo to node_modules/.cache/tsc, so a
    repeat typecheck skips re-checking unchanged lib .d.ts files. CI starts cold and
    is unaffected.

diff --git a/plugins/source-control/package.json b/plugins/source-control/package.json
index 192f656a5..26e873b17 100644
--- a/plugins/source-control/package.json
+++ b/plugins/source-control/package.json
@@ -95,7 +95,7 @@
     "dev": "bb plugin dev .",
     "build": "bb plugin build .",
     "lint": "oxlint",
-    "typecheck": "tsc --noEmit",
+    "typecheck": "tsc --noEmit --incremental --tsBuildInfoFile ../../node_modules/.cache/tsc/plugins-source-control.tsbuildinfo",
     "test": "vitest run --config vitest.config.ts",
     "clean": "rm -rf dist"
   }

commit 7592ac8401ecc261722012115a8f463b8ccf9f30
Author: Scott Sunarto <github@smsunarto.com>
Date:   Sun Nov 15 22:03:08 2026 -0800

    fix(source-control): harden PR image resolution after review
    
    - Image reads try every gh account and never change which account bb
      remembers for a repository (F2).
    - A committed file's ref may hold slashes: the PR's head and base branches
      are tried first, then up to four splits; LFS's media host is accepted (F3, F7).
    - Signed reads queue per repository; a request waits at most 8 s, then answers
      the failed state while the shared read finishes for the next load (F4, F5).
    - The rewrite is one bounded linear scan that skips code, suggestion blocks,
      comments and escapes, and balances parentheses in a destination (F8, F11).
    - Results are cached per image identity and repository, not per URL (F9).
    - An image never shown to be private goes to its own URL when no account can
      sign it (F10, partial: the app does not know repository visibility).
    - No permanent minimum size on routed images (F6).
    - The description test renders the rewritten Markdown and checks real images.

